 [:option {:value "2010900"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/278"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Foil, Individual, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "26 July 2021"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2125"} "Makuhari Messe, 2-1, Nakase, Mihama-ku, Chiba, Chiba Prefecture, Japan"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/19016400"} "35 from 18 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single-elimination tournament."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Italy’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/134617"} "Daniele Garozzo"] " was the defending gold medalist but he had only one medal individually at the World Championships, a bronze in 2017. The last three World Championships had been won by three different fencers – " [:a {:href "/athletes/1100157"} "Dmitry Zherebchenko"] " (RUS) in 2017, " [:a {:href "/athletes/144175"} "Alessio Foconi"] " (ITA) in 2018, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/120056"} "Enzo Lefort"] " (FRA) in 2019, although Zherebchenko was not present in Tokyo. The #1 seed was the United States’ " [:a {:href "/athletes/118199"} "Gerek Meinhardt"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Meinhardt did not last long, losing his first match to " [:a {:href "/athletes/146246"} "Vladislav Mylnikov"] " (ROC), the #33 seed. Garozzo and Lefort advanced to the quarter-finals, where they would face each other. Foconi lost in the round of 16 to " [:a {:href "/athletes/134324"} "Edgar Cheung"] " of Hong Kong, China, who had little international experience outside of Asia, and was seeded 15th."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Garozzo handled Lefort easily in the quarters and he and Cheung would advance to the finals. Cheung won the final in an upset, defeating Garozzo 15-11. He would come back at Paris 2024 and defend his gold medal, something only done twice before, by " [:a {:href "/athletes/22697"} "Nedo Nadi"] " (ITA) in 1912-20 and " [:a {:href ""} "Christian d’Oriola"] " (FRA) in 1952-56."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Seed"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "15"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/134324"} "Edgar Cheung"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HKG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HKG.png"}] "HKG"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "5"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/134617"} "Daniele Garozzo"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "19"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/133423"} "Alexander Choupenitch"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CZE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CZE.png"}] "CZE"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "9"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/144615"} "Takahiro Shikine"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "5"] [:td {:class "bib"} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/120056"} "Enzo Lefort"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :sr